      "notes": "Through-host aperture for the original curtain-wall door 2471813 between 10-1300 Vestibule and the 10-1302 Atrium. Same-host jamb mullions 2471836/2471837 with sill 2471832 and head 2471834 keep the door's native clear width across curtain host 2471383. Basic wall 2472128 is listed because its plan cut is drawn across the door band although its native body is cut where the curtain wall is embedded. Derived from native evidence only (source-evidence case 1, 2026-11-02; validator replay 2026-11-16). Requested by the owner on 2026-11-16; that the door is normally open and public, any partition on the 2472128 line, and the modelled 50 mm sill are not confirmed on site, and room access stays as recorded. Depth revised on 2026-11-16: from the near face of jamb mullions 2471836/2471837 (762.393) to the far face of the approximate band (764.280). In the first rebuild (master 40587dd7) the full-band aperture left a 1.39 ft strip on the vestibule side that belonged to neither native cell 481 nor the indoor envelope, so the vestibule portal (on the registered outline at 762.514) could not join the room and 10-1300 kept no arrival. Not yet replayed in a rebuild."
